60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Looking at the candidates, the Central Study Commons seems to align best with my findings on general-use spaces and avoids the mechanical risks Benjamin mentioned.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I agree with Toshio. The Central Study Commons provides broad utility and, as a conversion of an underused hall, likely avoids the severe room-closure costs I found.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"The Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade is the only option that directly addresses the manual burdens of the technicians, which is a critical issue for our staff's sustainability.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I must disagree with George; the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade involves the very mechanical plant costs Benjamin warned about and likely the hazardous materials I found in older blocks, making it a high-risk choice.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""George"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Mizuki makes a compelling point. The ventilation project is a financial and scheduling gamble, whereas the Study Commons appears far more stable and fiscally predictable.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, while I sympathize with the staff, the data suggests that a project limited to a single wing, like the labs, often yields the lowest overall satisfaction for the campus.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@George, I must also point out that the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade would likely take several rooms out of service, leading to the expensive off-site rentals I discovered.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"I understand the risks, but we are neglecting the people who keep this university running. If we ignore the technicians' daily struggle, we are simply choosing a convenient project over a necessary one.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, necessity is only useful if it is achievable. A project that stalls for a year due to hazardous materials or budget overruns provides no relief to the staff and wastes our capital.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a classic dilemma of urgency versus feasibility. However, the risk of a project that fails to deliver is a far greater disservice to the staff than choosing a more reliable alternative.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I believe the Central Study Commons is the most rational choice, as it maximizes campus-wide benefit while minimizing the operational and financial risks we have all identified.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I concur. The Study Commons offers a high-utility, low-disruption solution that respects both our budget and our operational constraints.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"I cannot in good conscience support a project that ignores the technicians' manual burdens, but I recognize the weight of the risks you all have presented.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I believe the Central Study Commons is the only candidate that avoids the hazardous material risks and the scheduling slips associated with comfort-based projects in older blocks.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I agree. Given the evidence of rising plant costs and the lack of reserves, the Study Commons is the only fiscally responsible choice that ensures we actually deliver a result.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for the Central Study Commons.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for the Central Study Commons.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,I vote for the Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I vote for the Central Study Commons.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for the Central Study Commons.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
